course: dictionary
lesson: 9333
title: Spinal: the backbone and its cord
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Spinal is an adjective. It means to do with the spine, which is the backbone, or with the spinal cord inside it. Look at the word: spine plus -al, so it describes something linked to the spine. «It sits inside the skull and is joined to the spinal cord, which runs down inside the backbone.» Here spinal tells you the cord belongs to the backbone.
explain: Context helps you spot spinal in a sentence. «A reflex is a quick automatic movement: in the knee-jerk test the signal goes to the spinal cord and straight back to the muscle without waiting for the brain.» The words around spinal cord tell you it is a part of the body that handles messages.
explain: Spinal can also describe serious harm. «A spinal injury» means damage to the spine or the spinal cord, and it is very serious. Phrases such as spinal column and spinal cord always point back to the backbone.
fact: Spinal means to do with the spine (backbone) or the spinal cord.
fact: The spinal cord is a thick bundle of nerves inside the backbone.
fact: The spinal cord carries messages between the brain and the body.
fact: The spine protects the spinal cord.
fact: Animals with a spine are called vertebrates.
exercise: «It sits inside the skull and is joined to the spinal cord, which runs down inside the backbone.» What does spinal mean here? | To do with the stomach | *To do with the backbone | To do with the ears | To do with the heart
exercise: What is the spinal cord? | A muscle in the arm | A blood vessel in the head | *A thick bundle of nerves inside the backbone | A bone in the leg
exercise: A «spinal injury» is very serious. What should you do if someone may have hurt their back or neck? | Ask them to stand up | Give them a drink | Move them quickly to a chair | *Call for help and do not move them
test: Which animals are vertebrates? | Animals with no bones at all | *Animals with a spine | Animals with a shell only | Animals with wings only
test: «A reflex is a quick action where the message goes to the spinal cord.» Why does the message go to the spinal cord? | It stores the messages for later | It carries the message to the stomach | *It sends the order straight back without waiting for the brain | It makes the heart beat faster
exam: Where is the spinal cord found? | In the stomach | Under the skin of the arm | *Inside the backbone | In the chest, around the heart
